From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:25:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: optional list of local ports peers may reach
 (TS_KILN_ALLOWED_PORTS)

Kiln OS patch for kiln-tailscale. In userspace networking mode, TCP and
UDP from peers to this node's Tailscale addresses are passed on to the
same port on 127.0.0.1, so peers reach every local port. When
TS_KILN_ALLOWED_PORTS is set and not empty (ports separated by commas
or spaces), only those ports are passed on: TCP to other ports gets a
RST without dialing 127.0.0.1, UDP to other ports is dropped. Entries
that are not ports 1-65535 are skipped, so a list without a valid port
allows none. Unset or empty: upstream behaviour.

Signed-off-by: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 wgengine/netstack/netstack.go           |  22 ++++
 wgengine/netstack/netstack_kiln.go      |  46 ++++++++
 wgengine/netstack/netstack_kiln_test.go | 142 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 210 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wgengine/netstack/netstack_kiln.go
 create mode 100644 wgengine/netstack/netstack_kiln_test.go

